<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishar-damu"><span class="enc-name">Ishar-Damu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ishar-Damu was the last king of Ebla documented in the archives of its palace, reigning in the twenty-fourth century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishbi-erra"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ishbi-erra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ishbi-Erra</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ishbi-Erra was the founder of the First Dynasty of Isin, ruling about 2017–1985 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishhi-addu"><span class="enc-name">Ishhi-Addu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ishhi-Addu was king of Qatna in western Syria in the early 18th century BCE, known from the archives of Mari.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishida-mitsunari"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ishida-mitsunari.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ishida Mitsunari</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ishida Mitsunari was a Japanese warlord and administrator, one of the five commissioners who ran the government of Toyotomi Hideyoshi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishikawa-prefecture"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ishikawa-prefecture.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ishikawa Prefecture</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ishikawa Prefecture is a prefecture of Japan on the Sea of Japan coast of Honshu, in the Hokuriku region, with its capital at Kanazawa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishkhani"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ishkhani.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ishkhani</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Ishkhani is a medieval Georgian monastery and cathedral in the historic region of Tao, today the village of İşhan in Artvin Province, north-eastern Turkey.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishkhara"><span class="enc-name">Ishkhara</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Ishkhara was a goddess of the ancient Near East, worshipped at Ebla in Syria from the third millennium BCE and later in Mesopotamia and among the Hurrians and Hittites.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishme-dagan-i"><span class="enc-name">Ishme-Dagan I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ishme-Dagan I was the elder son of Shamshi-Adad I, the Amorite ruler of the Kingdom of Upper Mesopotamia, in the 18th century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishpabara"><span class="enc-name">Ishpabara</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ishpabara was a king of Ellipi in the central Zagros in the late 8th century BCE, son of Dalta.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishpakai"><span class="enc-name">Ishpakai</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ishpakai was the earliest known Scythian king, named in Assyrian texts from the reign of Esarhaddon as ruler of Ishkuza in north-western Iran.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishpuini"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ishpuini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ishpuini</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ishpuini was king of Urartu in the late ninth century BCE, the son of Sarduri I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ishtar-gate"><img clas